# Purpose and audience: executable specification evidence for the owning engineering team.
# @req REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
# research: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; design: doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md

# @req REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM NFR-001 NFR-002 NFR-003 NFR-004 NFR-005 NFR-006 NFR-007 NFR-008 NFR-009 NFR-010 NFR-012
"""

**Feature IDs:** #NVME-COSMOS-001
**Category:** Hardware
**Difficulty:** 4/5
**Status:** Implemented (bring-up; silicon port gaps enumerated)
**Plan:** doc/03_plan/hardware/cosmos_openssd_port_2026-06-30.md
**Research:** doc/01_research/hardware/nvme_firmware/research_addendum_2026-06-29.md

Config 3: the real NVMe-fw dev environment based on the CRZ Cosmos+ OpenSSD platform. The
Cortex-A9 bring-up (`src/os/kernel/arch/arm32/cosmos/`, Cadence UART) boots on QEMU's
`xilinx-zynq-a9` and prints a banner plus an explicit "MISSING for silicon" gap list — the
port is deliberately incomplete and says so (see the plan doc for the full gap analysis).

Build the image first: `sh src/os/kernel/arch/arm32/cosmos/build.shs`.

## Syntax

Run only with `bin/release/simple` rebuilt and deployed from the current tree
in interpreter mode. A stale release runner with the obsolete `rt_env_set` ABI
can crash before any scenario executes and is not evidence.

## Examples

`bin/release/simple test test/03_system/app/nvme_firmware/nvme_cosmos_openssd_boot_spec.spl --mode=interpreter`

## Claim Boundary

Passing proves hardware-independent host and QEMU behavior, exact silicon
profile compilation, ELF identity, and package validation. It does not prove
physical NAND IO/ECC, PCIe enumeration/MSI/DMA/reset, CPU1 coherency, BootROM
boot, power-loss recovery, thermal behavior, or endurance. The board-only
requirements REQ-012 and NFR-011 are excluded from `@req` and remain pending
until retained evidence from the identified board satisfies the production
guide. The NVMe callback-service scenario does not bind real PCIe/NFC adapters
and is not board evidence. The current strict bootstrap reached Stage 3, but
its third/final Stage 4 attempt was terminated at about 64 GiB RSS; no current
`bin/release/simple` exists and this spec has not been executed or doc-generated.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.io_runtime.{process_run}
use app.io.mod.{file_read_text}
use os.kernel.arch.arm32.cosmos.cosmos_fsbl_decision.cosmos_fsbl_handoff_valid_registers

val BUILD: text = "src/os/kernel/arch/arm32/cosmos/build.shs"
val PACKAGE: text = "src/os/kernel/arch/arm32/cosmos/package_boot.shs"
val HOST_MMIO: text = "test/02_integration/os/cosmos/run_cosmos_hal_mmio_test.shs"
val FSBL_VECTORS: text = "test/fixtures/os/cosmos/fsbl_handoff_vectors.tsv"
val HOST_ABORT: text = "test/02_integration/os/cosmos/run_cosmos_abort_contract_test.shs"
val HOST_RUNTIME: text = "test/02_integration/os/cosmos/run_cosmos_runtime_contract_test.shs"
val HOST_NVME: text = "test/02_integration/os/cosmos/run_cosmos_nvme_firmware_contract_test.shs"
val HOST_FTL: text = "test/02_integration/os/cosmos/run_cosmos_ftl_contract_test.shs"
